      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Founded as Snoqualmie Prairie in 1889, the town was later renamed North Bend after the nearby bend in the Snoqualmie River.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7,
        8
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/North_Bend%2C_Washington",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "After Weyerhaeuser’s sawmill closed, North Bend evolved into a thriving bedroom community for Seattle and Bellevue.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        16
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/North_Bend%2C_Washington",
      "category": "economy",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The Snoqualmie Indian Tribe has lived in the prairie that now forms North Bend for thousands of years.",
